To create a chat app using Transformers.js with the Facebook BlenderBot model, you'll need to follow these steps:

1. **Set up your project**: Create a new directory for your project and initialize it as an npm package.

2. **Install dependencies**: Install `transformers` and any other necessary packages like `axios` or `react` if needed.

3. **Load the model**: Use Transformers.js to load the BlenderBot model.

4. **Create the UI**: Build a simple HTML page with input fields and buttons for user interaction.

5. **Handle user input**: Capture user messages and send them to the model.

6. **Display responses**: Show the generated response from the model back to the user.

Here’s a step-by-step guide on how to do this:

### Step 1: Set Up Your Project

```bash
mkdir blenderbot-chat-app
cd blenderbot-chat-app
npm init -y
```

### Step 2: Install Dependencies

```bash
npm install @huggingface/transformers axios
```

### Step 3: Load the Model

Create a file named `index.js` and add the following code to load the BlenderBot model:

```javascript
import { AutoTokenizer, AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM } from '@huggingface/transformers';

const tokenizer = await AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained('facebook/blenderbot-400m-distill');
const model = await AutoModelForSeq2SeqLM.from_pretrained('facebook/blenderbot-400m-distill');

export { tokenizer, model };
```

### Step 4: Create the UI

Create an `index.html` file with the following content:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>BlenderBot Chat App</title>
    <style>
        body {
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            margin: 20px;
        }
        #chat-container {
            width: 400px;
            border: 1px solid #ccc;
            padding: 10px;
            height: 300px;
            overflow-y: scroll;
        }
        .message {
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }
        .user-message {
            text-align: right;
            color: blue;
        }
        .bot-message {
            text-align: left;
            color: green;
        }
        input[type="text"] {
            width: calc(100% - 22px);
            padding: 10px;
            box-sizing: border-box;
        }
        button {
            padding: 10px;
            background-color: #007bff;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            cursor: pointer;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div id="chat-container"></div>
    <input type="text" id="user-input" placeholder="Type your message here...">
    <button onclick="sendMessage()">Send</button>

    <script src="./index.js"></script>
    <script>
        const chatContainer = document.getElementById('chat-container');
        const userInput = document.getElementById('user-input');

        async function sendMessage() {
            const userMessage = userInput.value.trim();
            if (!userMessage) return;

            // Add user message to chat container
            appendMessage(userMessage, 'user-message');

            // Send message to server (or directly process)
            try {
                const response = await generateResponse(userMessage);
                appendMessage(response, 'bot-message');
            } catch (error) {
                console.error('Error generating response:', error);
                appendMessage('Sorry, there was an error processing your request.', 'bot-message');
            }

            userInput.value = '';
        }

        function appendMessage(message, className) {
            const div = document.createElement('div');
            div.className = `message ${className}`;
            div.textContent = message;
            chatContainer.appendChild(div);
            chatContainer.scrollTop = chatContainer.scrollHeight;
        }

        async function generateResponse(inputText) {
            const inputs = tokenizer.encode(inputText, { return_tensors: 'pt' });
            const outputs = await model.generate(inputs);
            return tokenizer.decode(outputs[0], { skip_special_tokens: true });
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

